      "content": "Thanks, that's a decent start. It's a bit dense, but it flows okay. \n\nActually, looking at the pre-screening tool again, it's flagging my current draft as \"low alignment\" because the density is too low for the threshold. I need to beef this up. \n\nCan you expand this into a full page (maybe 3-4 paragraphs)? It needs to cover the technical challenges, the potential impact on future computing, and the urgency of the timeline. \n\nJust a reminder—please don't just list the keywords or make it repetitive just to satisfy the formula. If the reviewers see a high density of terms but no actual scientific substance or coherent argument, they'll reject it immediately. I need the argument to be strong, but I also really need to get that density score up so it actually makes it past the automated filter. Try to find a way to weave them in naturally so it stays professional.",
